{
  "id": "10_blackout_heist_2d",
  "title": "Blackout Heist",
  "genre": "2D top-down stealth heist",
  "orientation": 0,
  "startScene": "Main",
  "scenes": [
    "Main"
  ],
  "networking": false,
  "ai_assist": false,
  "scripts": [
    "Thief.js",
    "Guard.js",
    "Cam.js",
    "Loot.js",
    "Terminal.js",
    "Exit.js",
    "Heist.js",
    "Hud.js",
    "Burst.js",
    "Puff.js"
  ],
  "controls": {
    "axis": "left stick / WASD -- move (push further to run)",
    "Sneak": "toggle -- creep, quiet and much harder to spot",
    "Interact": "hold to take the keycard, crack a crate or safe, cut the camera feed, or climb into the van",
    "Interact (aftermath)": "start the run again"
  },
  "systems": [
    "grid-locked movement with script-owned collision and prop blocking",
    "guard vision: range, cone (wider up close), and an exact line of sight walk over the level grid",
    "per-guard detection meter drawn above the guard, feeding a shared alarm",
    "light as a gameplay value: a lamp pool is the radius guards can see you in",
    "noise: running is heard through walls, creeping is not",
    "three sweeping eyes -- two cameras and the dock searchlight -- and one terminal that blinds the grid for the rest of the run",
    "hold-to-interact chain: keycard, three vault crates, the van",
    "procedurally carved rooms with a connectivity proof in the builder"
  ],
  "engineNotes": {
    "notes": [
      "The level grid is baked into Thief.js, Guard.js and Cam.js as a string table -- '.' open, 'x' blocked by a prop, '#' wall -- and all three are written from the same grid by tools/build_heist.py, so they cannot drift.",
      "The builder refuses to emit a level whose rooms are not connected, whose props block a patrol point, or whose objectives cannot be reached.",
      "There are no Light components in this scene: Scene.Light is read by Renderer3D only, so every lamp is an additive emitter whose drawn size is the radius the scripts test -- one number, one meaning, visible on screen.",
      "Movement is script-owned.  Wall runs carry Collider2D for the editor, but the actors test the baked grid, because exact collision is what a stealth game is played on.",
      "Character animation comes from the RPG Top-Down pack's 128x256 sheets: rows 0-3 are the idle poses for down/left/right/up and rows 4-7 the walk cycle for the same directions; the fourth cell of each row repeats the first, so the clips are three frames long.",
      "The HUD is laid out inside +/-6.6 x +/-4.8 because the runtime draws screen-space objects through a fixed +/-5-unit view, independent of the game camera (see SceneRenderer.drawScreenUI).",
      "Cast: the thief, Rook, Vale, Sable, and three sweeping eyes."
    ]
  },
